From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 08:26:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07061/11362] [outer-loop] Task 12: goal_bias degenerate-score
 self-audit (GAP-5703 fix)

Ships GAP-5703's candidate design (a): StepwiseExplorer.goal_bias_diagnostics()
now surfaces the same class of degenerate-score self-audit
GoalEnergyCandidateGuidance already has (arms_non_degenerate), closing the
observability asymmetry exp5703 found between the two mechanisms.

Implementation: streaming (sum/sum-of-squares/min/max, not a stored list, to
avoid unbounded memory on long episodes) variance tracking in
_goal_bias_score. goal_bias_diagnostics() reports score_variance/score_min/
score_max/degenerate (nodes_scored>=20 AND score_variance<=1e-12, mirroring
GoalEnergyCandidateGuidance's variance floor plus a minimum-sample guard
against a false-positive read on a short episode).

Observability only -- does not disable goal_bias mid-episode or change
search behavior. A constant score is already mathematically a no-op on
ordering (confirmed by exp5703's candidate_router_changed_order_count=0 /
goal_candidate_guidance's own no-op finding for the sibling mechanisms);
auto-disabling mid-episode would be a separate, larger behavioral change
this fix deliberately does not attempt.

Verified directly against the real sp80 case that motivated it: after 4
nodes, degenerate=False (below the 20-sample floor); after a full
500-budget episode (938 real nodes), degenerate=True, score_variance=0.0,
score_min=score_max=1.0 -- reproducing exp5703's manually-found result now
available from the diagnostics dict directly.

Adds tests/python/test_arc_goal_bias_degeneracy_audit.py (6 tests) +
REQ-ARC-FCP-5703-2 spec.md section. The existing
test_experiment_4534_energy_trust_next_level_routing.py (only asserted
lower_is_better) passes unmodified.

